        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 501,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 523,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 502,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73156,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 502,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The brain may show multiple focal intraparenchymal lesions. Leptomeninges and cranial nerves may also be involved {16100084}. The spinal cord may also be affected {25983786}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 524,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 503,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73157,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 503,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This angiocentric and angiodestructive lymphoproliferative disorder affects the brain in 26% of patients, who may present with focal neurological symptoms and/or headache or cognitive impairment {16100084}. Presentation may even be indistinct from that of systemic manifestation {29635846; 31746046}. MRI may reveal mass lesions throughout the CNS {31746046}; multiple punctate lesions along perivascular and periventricular spaces have also been reported {29635846}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 525,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 504,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73158,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 504,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This rare disease usually manifests in adults in the fifth and sixth decade; a male predilection has been reported {761171; 9635846}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 526,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 505,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73159,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 505,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphomatoid granulomatosis is an EBV-driven disease. Immunodeficiency increases the risk of lymphomatoid granulomatosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 527,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 506,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73160,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 506,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Disease is hypothesized to result from defective immunosurveillance of EBV and an abnormal immune response towards EBV {32107539}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 534,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 513,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73161,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 513,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Macroscopically, the lesions may resemble tumour or infarct-like areas of necrosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 528,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 507,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73162,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 507,
        "headingText": "<p>Lesions are characterized by polymorphous lymphoid infiltrates consisting of lymphocytes (including CD4+ and CD8+ T lymphocytes), and plasma cells intermingled with varying numbers of atypical EBV+, CD20+, CD30+/&minus;, CD15&minus; large neoplastic B&nbsp;cells. Grading of lymphomatoid granulomatosis depends on the proportion of EBV-expressing CD20+ B&nbsp;cells (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/45/166/19016\" target=\"_blank\">#19016</a>Table&nbsp;10.01). Most cases affecting the CNS correspond to grade&nbsp;3, with large aggregates of EBV+ CD20+ B&nbsp;cells, and they should be classified as EBV+ diffuse large B-cell lymphoma of the CNS. The infiltrates invade blood vessel walls and may induce infarct-like necrosis of tumour and/or brain tissue. Rarely, CNS WHO grade&nbsp;2 lesions may occur in the CNS.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-10-25T14:50:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 529,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 508,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73163,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 508,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 530,
    "bookid": 45,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 509,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 73164,
        "bookId": 45,
        "chapterId": 166,
        "headingId": 509,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Detection of clonal rearrangement of IG genes may be helpful in diagnostically difficult cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2021-09-30T16:11:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
